IMPORT prelude

-- Interpretation Act 1965 (Singapore) -- computing time: the definitions of month and year (s 2), periods of days and the
-- days excluded from them (s 50), and standard time (s 51). And a negative finding: the Act has NO provision on when a
-- person attains an age.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IA1965.txt (version
-- in force from 5 December 2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0013 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl), raised three times by the cradle-to-grave-simone
-- scenario, asked this Act when a person born on 14 March 2003 attains 21. Every age test in every row depends on the
-- answer. Reading the Act found that it does not give one; see the "Attaining an age" section below and NOTES.md.
--
-- DAYS ARE NUMBERS. The installed l4 binary has no date library (IMPORT daydate does not resolve), so a day is a whole
-- number counted from day 0 = Monday 1 January 2024. Day n is a Sunday when n MODULO 7 is 6. Days before 2024 are not
-- supported by this convention. Public holidays are an input: up to three day numbers in a Calendar record, a day never
-- reached (such as 999999) for none.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: everything else in the Act (definitions other than month and year, construction of written laws,
-- subsidiary legislation, powers, references and citation).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Interpretation Act 1965 -- time`

§§ `2 -- month and year`

-- s 2: "'month' means calendar month"; "'year' means a year reckoned according to the Gregorian calendar". The Act gives
-- no method for counting a period of months or years; only what the units are.
GIVETH A STRING
`what a month is` MEANS "a calendar month"

GIVETH A STRING
`what a year is` MEANS "a year reckoned according to the Gregorian calendar"

§§ `50 -- days`

-- s 50: "In computing time for the purposes of any written law, unless the contrary intention appears -- (a) a period of
-- days from the happening of an event or the doing of any act or thing is deemed to be exclusive of the day on which the
-- event happens or the act or thing is done; (b) if the last day of the period is a Sunday or a public holiday (which days
-- are called in this section excluded days) the period includes the next following day not being an excluded day; (c) when
-- any act or proceeding is directed or allowed to be done or taken on a certain day, then, if that day happens to be an
-- excluded day, the act or proceeding is considered as done or taken in due time if it is done or taken on the next day
-- afterwards, not being an excluded day; (d) when any act or proceeding is directed or allowed to be done or taken within
-- any time not exceeding 6 days, excluded days must not be reckoned in the computation of the time."
--
-- Excluded days are Sundays and public holidays only. A Saturday is not an excluded day under s 50.
DECLARE Calendar HAS
    `public holiday one` IS A NUMBER
    `public holiday two` IS A NUMBER
    `public holiday three` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `day is a Sunday` d IF
    d MODULO 7 EQUALS 6

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, cal IS A Calendar
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `day is a public holiday in` d cal IF
        d EQUALS cal's `public holiday one`
    OR  d EQUALS cal's `public holiday two`
    OR  d EQUALS cal's `public holiday three`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, cal IS A Calendar
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `day is excluded in` d cal IF
    `day is a Sunday` d OR `day is a public holiday in` d cal

-- s 50(b), (c): the next day, from d itself onwards, that is not an excluded day.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, cal IS A Calendar
GIVETH A NUMBER
`first day not excluded from` d cal MEANS
    IF `day is excluded in` d cal
    THEN `first day not excluded from` (d PLUS 1) cal
    ELSE d

-- s 50(d): the day reached after counting n days after d, skipping excluded days.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, cal IS A Calendar
GIVETH A NUMBER
`day after counting clear days` n d cal MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN d
    ELSE IF `day is excluded in` (d PLUS 1) cal
         THEN `day after counting clear days` n (d PLUS 1) cal
         ELSE `day after counting clear days` (n MINUS 1) (d PLUS 1) cal

-- The last day of "a period of n days from" an event on day d. (a): the event day is not counted, so the period runs to
-- d + n. (b): if that day is excluded, the next day that is not. (d): for a time not exceeding 6 days, excluded days are
-- not counted at all.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, cal IS A Calendar
GIVETH A NUMBER
`last day of a period of days` n d cal MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 6
    THEN `day after counting clear days` n d cal
    ELSE `first day not excluded from` (d PLUS n) cal

-- s 50(c): an act directed to be done on a day that is excluded is in due time on the next day that is not.
GIVEN `day directed` IS A NUMBER, `day done` IS A NUMBER, cal IS A Calendar
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `act on a fixed day is in due time` `day directed` `day done` cal IF
        `day done` EQUALS `day directed`
    OR  (`day is excluded in` `day directed` cal AND `day done` EQUALS `first day not excluded from` `day directed` cal)

§§ `51 -- standard time`

-- s 51(1): an expression of time in a written law is "held to be standard time"; (2) "8 hours ... in advance of Coordinated
-- Universal Time", unless the President determines otherwise by Gazette notification.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`standard time hours ahead of UTC` MEANS 8

§§ `Attaining an age -- not in this Act`

-- No section of the deposited Act says when a person attains an age: the words "age", "aged", "attain", "attains",
-- "attained", "birth", "birthday" and "anniversary" do not appear anywhere in the deposited text. s 50 governs periods of DAYS only, and s 2 says only what a
-- month and a year are. The rule REQ-0013 expected ("the anniversary of birth, at the start of the day") is stated, Act by
-- Act, in seven other deposited Acts (Women's Charter, Central Provident Fund, CareShield Life, MediShield Life, Child
-- Development Co-Savings, Children and Young Persons, Social Residential Homes) and nowhere for written law generally.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act fixes when a person attains an age` IF FALSE
